1
00:00:41,959 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,767
SANGCHEON PORT

5
00:03:58,989 --> 00:04:05,120
EPISODE 9
THE SUSPECT

6
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:09,791
[server] Enjoy.

7
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:10,876
[customer] Thank you.

8
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:24,014
-[crash]
-[victim] Hey, let go!

9
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,474
Let go of me!

10
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,267
[attacker] What the hell? Are you crazy?

11
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,394
-[victim screams]
-Get up!

12
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:31,980
-[crashing]
-[victim] Let go and talk to me!

13
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:33,398
[attacker] I'm not letting you go!

14
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,406
[attacker] Hey.
Why didn't you pick up yesterday?

15
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:44,743
-[victim screams] Stop! Stop!
-[attacker] Huh? Hey, look at me!

16
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:46,036
[attacker] Look me in the eye. Look at me!

17
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:47,871
-[victim] Stop it!
-[attacker screams]

18
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,833
-[attacker] Damn it!
-Are you okay? Go.

19
00:04:57,589 --> 00:04:58,757
Who the hell are you?

20
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,051
What, do you know her?

21
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:06,389
Do you two know each other?
I'm asking you!

22
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:12,270
-You hit a woman?
-[attacker scoffs]

23
00:05:12,354 --> 00:05:14,314
[attacker] What? What's wrong with that?

24
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,358
I can't hit her? [screams]

25
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,451
You're out of your damn mind!

26
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,830
[customer] Arm behind your back!

27
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:32,249
-That was dangerous, damn it.
-[attacker screams]

28
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:35,335
[customer] You hit a woman
and tried to gouge my eyes out?

29
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:39,214
You live in Namcheon?
What are you doing all the way out here?

30
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:41,508
[attacker] Officer, help me!

31
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:42,926
-[customer] Hand it over.
-[attacker screams]

32
00:05:43,009 --> 00:05:44,427
[attacker] Wait!

33
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:49,391
This is Detective Hwang Myeongsu
from Gangwon Major Crimes.

34
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,976
I need you to run an ID check.

35
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,186
It's 890404…

36
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,940
[attacker] Wait, I…

37
00:05:58,108 --> 00:05:59,776
I didn't have a weapon on me.

38
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:00,944
Yes.

39
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:33,977
Oh, for crying out loud.

40
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,441
Hey.

41
00:06:41,693 --> 00:06:42,694
Where?

42
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:44,988
Sangcheon?

43
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:52,537
[Myeongsu] Hello, how's it going?

44
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:55,832
Yes. Could you let me through?

45
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:14,517
When did they find him?

46
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,733
[reporter] <i>An ambulance is stationed</i>
<i>at Sangcheon Beach,</i>

47
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,860
and police officers are bustling about.

48
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:27,614
Last night, Min Junho,
who was on the run and publicly wanted

49
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:31,576
on suspicion of multiple sexual assaults,
was found dead on this beach.

50
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:35,497
Police and fire authorities say
Min Junho's body was partially damaged

51
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,334
<i>by seawater and soil</i>
<i>when it was discovered.</i>

52
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:43,129
<i>The police believe his body washed ashore</i>

53
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:47,759
<i>and are looking into the possibility</i>
<i>that he took his own life.</i>

54
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,261
<i>At around 1:00 a.m. on the 18th,</i>

55
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:53,306
<i>Min was seen entering</i>
<i>the Sangcheon Port area alone,</i>

56
00:07:53,390 --> 00:07:55,892
<i>wearing a black jacket</i>
<i>and a hat that concealed his face.</i>

57
00:07:56,434 --> 00:08:00,647
<i>He was reportedly wearing the same clothes</i>
<i>in the security footage</i>

58
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,316
<i>as when his body was discovered.</i>

59
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:08,571
<i>A police official said</i>
<i>there were few indications of foul play</i>

60
00:08:08,655 --> 00:08:11,449
<i>but stressed that</i>
<i>further investigation is needed.</i>

61
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:13,451
-[door unlocks]
-[Seokgu] Good morning.

62
00:08:13,535 --> 00:08:16,996
Did you go for a run?
You were already gone when I woke up.

63
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,540
Yeah.

64
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:19,999
It's become a habit.

65
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:24,045
You haven't eaten yet, right?
I'll make you breakfast.

66
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:35,724
Min Junho is dead.

67
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:40,603
Good.

68
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:45,316
No one will have to go through that now.

69
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:53,074
He never apologized to anyone, though.

70
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:57,537
[reporter on TV] <i>Mr. Min, a doctor at</i>
<i>a prestigious university hospital,</i>

71
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,415
<i>was suspected of drugging</i>
<i>and sexually assaulting</i>

72
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,917
<i>at least nine people.</i>

73
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:06,129
<i>Police say his victims</i>
<i>included a teacher at his son's school,</i>

74
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,630
-<i>a nurse at the same hospital…</i>
-[door opens]

75
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:10,967
<i>…and even a police officer</i>
<i>investigating the case.</i>

76
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:15,305
<i>Police will continue investigating</i>
<i>the circumstances of Mr. Min's death.</i>

77
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:19,267
<i>However, with Mr. Min, who was suspected</i>
<i>of serial sexual assaults, found dead,</i>

78
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:24,939
<i>the case is now</i>
<i>likely to be closed without prosecution.</i>

79
00:09:25,023 --> 00:09:28,026
<i>-This is Kim Seonu for MBK News.</i>
-[phone buzzing]

80
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:35,492
Hello?

81
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,786
Namu, are you heading to work already?

82
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,205
I left early to beat the traffic.

83
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:42,832
<i>Did you see the news?</i>

84
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:43,917
What news?

85
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:48,338
Min Junho was found dead.

86
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,174
[Jisun] Oh…

87
00:09:52,634 --> 00:09:53,843
Yes, I saw.

88
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,515
They're saying he took his own life.

89
00:10:01,643 --> 00:10:03,061
[Jisun] I can't believe it.

90
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,647
[Namu] <i>It's finally all over.</i>

91
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,357
<i>You don't have to worry anymore.</i>

92
00:10:10,485 --> 00:10:11,986
<i>You're free tonight, right?</i>

93
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:14,155
Let's get together.

94
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:17,367
It's your first day back at work.
We should celebrate.

95
00:10:19,077 --> 00:10:20,078
Okay.

96
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:21,704
[Namu] <i>See you later.</i>

97
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,602
All right, let's get started.

98
00:10:49,858 --> 00:10:51,568
-Photos.
-[camera clicking]

99
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:21,389
-Hello!
-Hello!

100
00:11:26,895 --> 00:11:27,979
[student 1] Ms. Kang!

101
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:31,149
It's our first class of the semester.
Let's have some fun!

102
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,818
-[student 2] Yeah, exactly!
-[student 3] Let's have fun!

103
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:36,946
That's strange.
I thought we were playing make-believe.

104
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:39,282
STORY ADAPTATION CLASS
SISTER SUN AND BROTHER MOON

105
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,825
Not buying it, huh?

106
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:42,660
[student] In the original story,

107
00:11:42,744 --> 00:11:44,954
they go up to the sky
and become the sun and moon,

108
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:47,290
and the tiger falls to his death

109
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:49,667
-when the rope turns out to be rotten.
-[Jisun] Right.

110
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:53,546
[student] But in my version, the brother
and sister get revenge on the tiger.

111
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:56,549
How? Why don't you turn around
and tell the class?

112
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:57,675
[student] Sure.

113
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:02,472
They pretend to fall for the tiger's trick
when he says he's their mother.

114
00:12:03,056 --> 00:12:06,851
They say, "Mother, could you
fetch us some water from the well?"

115
00:12:06,935 --> 00:12:08,186
"Then we'll open the door."

116
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:21,908
Ms. Kang Jisun?

117
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,497
Can I help you?

118
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:36,798
I'm Section Chief Hwang Myeongsu
from Gangwon Major Crimes.

119
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:45,515
Min Junho's body

120
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,600
was found last night.

121
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:54,649
I saw it on the news.

122
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:58,069
[Myeongsu] The tide usually
carries bodies out to sea,

123
00:12:58,152 --> 00:12:59,862
but his washed back ashore.

124
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:08,329
When did he die?

125
00:13:10,248 --> 00:13:14,127
Forensics estimates he died early
the day before yesterday.

126
00:13:20,091 --> 00:13:21,342
The two of you…

127
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:27,056
had quite the history, didn't you?

128
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:33,396
I'm just one of his victims.

129
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:38,109
You know what kind of man Min Junho was,
don't you?

130
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:50,121
[Myeongsu] You were the first and only one
to report Min Junho.

131
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:53,374
Then he even accused you
of making false allegations.

132
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,757
And on top of that,

133
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:04,719
you found evidence of his crimes yourself
and took it to the police.

134
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:06,929
Exactly.

135
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:10,266
I even found evidence,
but the police couldn't catch him.

136
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:14,103
When was the last time you saw him?

137
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:20,943
-I've already told the police.
-I heard the gist of it.

138
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:23,738
But as it happens,

139
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:26,908
you were the only person who saw him
after we put out a wanted notice,

140
00:14:27,909 --> 00:14:29,410
so I'd like to hear more about it.

141
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:36,584
He could've escaped.

142
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:40,463
Instead, he took the risk
of staying in Sangcheon

143
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,673
and showed up again,
right in front of you.

144
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:48,429
While being chased by the police,

145
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:53,476
why do you think
he recklessly attempted to kill you?

146
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:55,895
-[Jisun struggling]

147
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:05,238
Probably because I was the one
who found the evidence.

148
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,920
[Jisun] I don't want to pretend

149
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:24,423
it's a shame that he died
and I lost the chance to forgive him.

150
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:25,675
Min Junho…

151
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,721
He paid the price for what he did.

152
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:38,896
Ms. Kang Jisun.

153
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:44,277
Who do you think killed Min Junho?

154
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:52,034
I thought he took his own life.

155
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:54,287
[Myeongsu] At first,
given the circumstances,

156
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:55,663
we did suspect he took his own life.

157
00:15:56,164 --> 00:16:00,126
[pathologist] There's a stab wound
to the heart, eight centimeters deep,

158
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:02,670
penetrating the anterior wall
of the right ventricle.

159
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,006
Given its location, it's certainly fatal.

160
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,924
And if you look here,

161
00:16:07,008 --> 00:16:10,469
there's foam in the trachea and bronchi,
and fluid in the lungs.

162
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:13,639
This suggests he may have drowned.

163
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:17,101
This suggests he inhaled water
while still alive,

164
00:16:17,602 --> 00:16:20,479
rather than simply
being submerged after death.

165
00:16:22,315 --> 00:16:23,482
Okay, so?

166
00:16:24,442 --> 00:16:26,444
What was the actual cause of death?

167
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:29,238
The stab wound or drowning?

168
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:32,825
It's still too early to say for sure.

169
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:39,248
Then someone must have stabbed Min Junho
in the heart and…

170
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:45,504
We believe he was thrown into the sea
before his heart stopped beating.

171
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:50,843
The person who killed Min Junho…

172
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:53,971
Who could it be?

173
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:03,314
There were plenty of people
who wanted Min Junho dead.

174
00:17:05,483 --> 00:17:08,611
I don't know who did it and I don't care.

175
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:12,240
But as one of his victims,
I hope whoever did it never gets caught.

176
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:20,998
The one who drove him to his death
was Min Junho himself.

177
00:17:24,627 --> 00:17:28,214
What were you doing around three or four
in the morning two days ago?

178
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:29,674
I was asleep at home.

179
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,593
Is there anyone who can confirm that
or any other proof of it?

180
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:38,558
Unfortunately,
I didn't film myself sleeping.

181
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:44,981
Right.

182
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:49,527
I understand.

183
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:54,156
Anything else you'd like to tell me?

184
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:58,953
It's all over now.

185
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:06,002
I don't want to hear
or know anything more about Min Junho.

186
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:13,134
I have a class to teach soon.

187
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,641
Thank you for your cooperation.

188
00:18:21,142 --> 00:18:22,268
Of course.

189
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,021
[Myeongsu] Ms. Kang Jisun.

190
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,445
It isn't over until it's over.

191
00:18:34,614 --> 00:18:36,657
If anything, this is just the beginning.

192
00:18:42,163 --> 00:18:43,998
Because we still have to catch the killer.

193
00:19:07,188 --> 00:19:09,940
MIN JUNHO
AUG 20, 2026

194
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,984
-[knocking]
-Yes.

195
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,862
Chief Hwang.

196
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,325
I'm Jang Duil
of Women and Juvenile Affairs.

197
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,494
I heard you wanted to meet.

198
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:33,172
Honestly, I thought our station
would handle the case.

199
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:36,926
So I was surprised to see
the Regional Major Crimes Unit here.

200
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:44,558
The only person who reported the culprit
responsible for nine sexual assaults

201
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:46,560
was accused of making a false report,

202
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:48,896
and the victim herself
had to find the evidence.

203
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,775
It nearly got thrown out
as illegally obtained

204
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,277
if Min Junho's mother hadn't confirmed it.

205
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:58,447
And after he went missing
following a failed arrest,

206
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,658
he was found murdered
right here in this area

207
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,577
just nine days after being publicly named
as a wanted suspect.

208
00:20:07,957 --> 00:20:10,376
Do you have any objections
to me taking over this case?

209
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:19,719
Starting today, you'll be working with me.

210
00:20:19,802 --> 00:20:22,388
I'm not assigned to homicide cases.

211
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:25,224
-You should talk with--
-You know this case better than anyone.

212
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:29,979
You know the people involved
and this area well.

213
00:20:31,439 --> 00:20:34,859
In fact, the report's already been filed
and approved.

214
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:44,910
How far along are you

215
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:47,705
in interviewing the victims
and others connected to the case?

216
00:20:48,456 --> 00:20:49,665
Well…

217
00:20:51,459 --> 00:20:53,377
We were focused on finding Min Junho.

218
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:55,463
So, we haven't…

219
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,098
We'd have nothing to say

220
00:21:06,182 --> 00:21:09,393
if people accused the police
of aiding and abetting murder.

221
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:25,242
Do you think the culprit we're looking for
could be among them?

222
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:29,121
They're all victims of Min Junho.

223
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:32,500
Listen, Mr. Regional Investigation Unit.

224
00:21:32,583 --> 00:21:35,419
These people are still recovering
from what they've been through.

225
00:21:35,503 --> 00:21:39,924
From now on, leave your sympathy
for the victims at home.

226
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:45,679
What you need to remember is that
this is a murder investigation.

227
00:21:45,763 --> 00:21:47,890
But still,

228
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,892
you can't treat the victims as suspects--

229
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:51,602
With the strongest motive for murder…

230
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:57,149
she's our prime suspect.

231
00:21:58,484 --> 00:22:00,319
Do you really suspect her?

232
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:03,113
Sometimes those doubts
are exactly what lead us to the culprit.

233
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:07,868
Of course,
if you'd arrested Min Junho in time,

234
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:10,830
Kang Jisun

235
00:22:11,914 --> 00:22:14,041
would still be just a victim.

236
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,085
KANG JISUN, 36
ASSAULTED MARCH 19, 2026

237
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:21,715
I should have made sure
to put him in cuffs.

238
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:23,175
Exactly.

239
00:22:23,259 --> 00:22:26,720
Then Min Junho wouldn't have ended up
washing ashore dead.

240
00:22:54,999 --> 00:22:57,001
<i>Parts of the coast are currently</i>

241
00:22:57,084 --> 00:23:00,963
<i>experiencing heavy downpours accompanied</i>
<i>by sudden gusts and strong winds.</i>

242
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:04,592
7 DAYS BEFORE MIN JUNHO'S DEATH

243
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:08,053
<i>…some areas are seeing</i>
<i>torrential rainfall.</i>

244
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:12,975
<i>Coastal roads and low-lying areas are</i>
<i>particularly vulnerable to flash flooding.</i>

245
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,477
<i>Drivers traveling at night</i>
<i>are advised to drive slowly</i>

246
00:23:15,561 --> 00:23:17,771
<i>and maintain a safe following distance.</i>

247
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:03,859
Are you going somewhere?

248
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:10,032
There's an emergency at the hospital.

249
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:11,700
They want me in as soon as possible.

250
00:24:17,039 --> 00:24:18,207
I won't be long.

251
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:24,338
Hyunsoo.

252
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,011
You're okay, right?

253
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,264
Where's this coming from?

254
00:24:35,224 --> 00:24:36,475
Well, I mean…

255
00:24:37,351 --> 00:24:39,436
Are you doing okay at school,
being on your own?

256
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,148
Dad, is something wrong?

257
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,865
Did you drink again?

258
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:55,160
-I love you, son.

259
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:12,886
Dad.

260
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:17,683
It's raining really hard.

261
00:25:18,642 --> 00:25:19,810
Be careful.

262
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:24,773
I will.

263
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:49,840
What's going on over there?

264
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:51,383
[detective] Looks like an accident.

265
00:25:51,467 --> 00:25:52,634
[Duil] Damn it.

266
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:54,511
Try going around.

267
00:25:54,595 --> 00:25:55,596
[detective] Yes, sir.

268
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,279
ACCIDENT CLEARANCE IN PROGRESS
TRAFFIC CONTROL

269
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:14,406
[officer] May I help you?

270
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:16,867
I'm Jang Duil from Sangcheon Police.
Let us through.

271
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:18,035
[officer] Yes. Got it, sir.

272
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,002
Man, what happened over there?

273
00:26:41,225 --> 00:26:43,727
SANGCHEON PORT

274
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,540
Is your dad home?

275
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:49,293
Why do you ask?

276
00:28:31,418 --> 00:28:33,170
[Junho] Hey, Dr. Jeon. How have you been?

277
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:35,839
How are things these days?

278
00:28:35,923 --> 00:28:38,675
You're still practicing plastic surgery
in Shanghai, right?

279
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:45,766
[detective] Did you find anything?

280
00:28:47,225 --> 00:28:49,686
-He said he was going to the hospital.
-He's not there.

281
00:28:54,775 --> 00:28:57,110
When you came
to the police station last time,

282
00:28:58,528 --> 00:29:02,407
you said your dad was here
at home with you, didn't you?

283
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:08,455
I know why you lied.

284
00:29:09,998 --> 00:29:12,000
But telling me the truth

285
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:17,798
is the best way to keep things
from getting worse and help your dad.

286
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:23,470
I'll ask you again.

287
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:28,308
Where is your dad?

288
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:01,967
[Hyunsoo] <i>He said there was an emergency.</i>

289
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:11,018
And he asked if I was doing okay.

290
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:20,402
There's nothing in the house.
Looks like he packed and left in a hurry.

291
00:30:37,335 --> 00:30:38,587
Is this your dad's yacht?

292
00:31:30,472 --> 00:31:32,349
-[detective] Damn it.

293
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:38,313
-[Duil] Go check over there.
-[detective] Yes, sir.

294
00:31:46,905 --> 00:31:48,115
[whispering] Sir.

295
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:07,050
-[door rattles]
-[Duil] Min Junho!

296
00:32:07,134 --> 00:32:08,135
Police.

297
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:09,928
Open up.

298
00:32:12,597 --> 00:32:14,182
I'll count to three.

299
00:32:14,808 --> 00:32:19,896
-One, two, three.
-[sighs]

300
00:32:21,481 --> 00:32:22,983
Stand back from the door.

301
00:32:23,525 --> 00:32:24,734
-Go ahead.
-[detective] Yes, sir.

302
00:32:54,848 --> 00:32:55,849
[detective] It's empty.

303
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:58,894
[Duil] What the hell?

304
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:29,174
OUTSTANDING INTEGRITY IN PLASTIC SURGERY
DR. JEON SUNGKI

305
00:33:33,178 --> 00:33:34,346
[attorney] Have some water.

306
00:33:41,811 --> 00:33:42,938
Have you eaten?

307
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:50,654
Hold on.

308
00:33:56,534 --> 00:33:57,535
Hello?

309
00:34:02,666 --> 00:34:03,750
Go ahead. I'm alone now.

310
00:34:05,877 --> 00:34:07,963
-Where's Hyunsoo?
-[attorney] <i>He's in the kitchen.</i>

311
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:09,798
Want me to put him on?

312
00:34:11,925 --> 00:34:14,219
No. Just tell me how he's doing.

313
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:17,389
He looks completely lost.
How could he not be?

314
00:34:22,227 --> 00:34:23,812
Junho, you need to turn yourself in.

315
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:28,441
Probation is out of the question.
We'll need to put together a legal team.

316
00:34:28,525 --> 00:34:30,610
I'm saying it's going to cost money.

317
00:34:30,694 --> 00:34:31,987
I'm not going to trial.

318
00:34:33,530 --> 00:34:34,531
What?

319
00:34:35,282 --> 00:34:37,492
I should've just gotten
Kang Jisun thrown in jail.

320
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:38,410
Hey, Junho…

321
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:40,370
The reason things got this bad is all…

322
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:43,248
This isn't the time
to be thinking about that.

323
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:46,418
-[call disconnects]
-First, let's…

324
00:34:50,797 --> 00:34:52,507
[sighs] Crazy bastard.

325
00:35:03,977 --> 00:35:06,271
[automated voice] <i>The phone is turned off.</i>

326
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:08,732
<i>Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

327
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:09,858
<i>Call charges…</i>

328
00:35:14,988 --> 00:35:16,323
[Hyunsoo] Did you know?

329
00:35:21,411 --> 00:35:22,996
That my dad was lying?

330
00:35:26,541 --> 00:35:27,751
Honestly,

331
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:31,463
I don't even know anymore
what is or isn't true.

332
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:21,888
3 DAYS AFTER MIN JUNHO'S DEATH

333
00:36:46,788 --> 00:36:50,625
[Jisun] Namu, I don't think
I can have dinner with you tonight.

334
00:36:50,709 --> 00:36:53,002
[Namu] <i>Why? Is something wrong?</i>

335
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:55,380
I'm not feeling very well.

336
00:36:56,381 --> 00:36:59,634
[Namu] <i>Well, I guess you haven't been able</i>
<i>to sleep well</i>

337
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:01,594
<i>with everything that's been going on.</i>

338
00:37:02,679 --> 00:37:05,598
<i>Try to relax and get a good night's sleep.</i>

339
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:07,642
Thanks.

340
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:09,728
I'll call you tomorrow.

341
00:37:20,405 --> 00:37:21,489
[Jisun] Are you going out?

342
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:23,324
Yeah, but I've still got some time.

343
00:37:23,408 --> 00:37:25,368
Did you see the kids over the weekend?

344
00:37:26,286 --> 00:37:27,954
We went to an amusement park together.

345
00:37:28,037 --> 00:37:30,123
-Want something to drink?
-No.

346
00:37:30,206 --> 00:37:31,291
What about Hyeongsu?

347
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:34,753
He just dropped the kids off and left.

348
00:37:34,836 --> 00:37:36,212
How did he seem?

349
00:37:38,465 --> 00:37:39,632
Well,

350
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:43,803
he tries to act like he's doing fine,
at least in front of me.

351
00:38:00,278 --> 00:38:02,071
Did you hear about Min Junho?

352
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:06,201
Yeah, on the news.

353
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:08,161
The police came to see me.

354
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:11,956
Why?

355
00:38:13,583 --> 00:38:15,627
[Jisun] Just to ask me some questions
as a witness.

356
00:38:18,922 --> 00:38:20,173
They said he was murdered.

357
00:38:24,677 --> 00:38:26,262
Not that he took his own life?

358
00:38:30,517 --> 00:38:32,435
Hey, you deleted that text, right?

359
00:38:39,067 --> 00:38:43,363
There's no way
they'll find the phone, right?

360
00:38:45,865 --> 00:38:47,575
You know nothing, okay?

361
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:55,667
[Myeongsu] What were you doing
at the time of Min Junho's death?

362
00:39:08,429 --> 00:39:10,473
I was supervising patrols.

363
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:14,936
<i>After Min Junho</i>
<i>was put on the wanted list,</i>

364
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:21,150
<i>groups of civilian patrols</i>
<i>started patrolling vulnerable areas.</i>

365
00:39:23,278 --> 00:39:25,154
I volunteered
for weekend and night shifts,

366
00:39:26,698 --> 00:39:28,116
because I felt responsible.

367
00:39:29,784 --> 00:39:31,661
I see you were at the beach often.

368
00:39:34,205 --> 00:39:35,206
Yes.

369
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:39,335
I've gotten into the habit of
getting up around 5:00 a.m. to go jogging.

370
00:39:43,006 --> 00:39:45,300
[Myeongsu] Do you have anything
to back up your alibi?

371
00:39:47,677 --> 00:39:49,804
You can check the duty logs.

372
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:52,932
<i>There should be security footage</i>
<i>from the hospital too.</i>

373
00:39:58,187 --> 00:40:00,565
Did you ever step out, even briefly?

374
00:40:05,612 --> 00:40:07,030
A few times…

375
00:40:08,489 --> 00:40:10,325
<i>to go to the restroom outside.</i>

376
00:40:35,224 --> 00:40:37,977
Min Junho didn't take his own life.

377
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:42,565
He was murdered.

378
00:40:47,070 --> 00:40:48,112
Who…

379
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:51,157
Who…

380
00:40:53,868 --> 00:40:55,870
Who killed Min Junho?

381
00:40:58,748 --> 00:41:00,625
I guess he got what he deserved.

382
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:03,586
How would I know?

383
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:08,967
Does that matter?

384
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:11,761
[Hwayoung] <i>So you don't have</i>

385
00:41:13,179 --> 00:41:14,597
any evidence?

386
00:41:20,186 --> 00:41:23,272
[sighs] Hwayoung doesn't know that I know.

387
00:41:24,941 --> 00:41:29,070
So please keep it between us
that I was questioned and that I know.

388
00:41:31,197 --> 00:41:32,198
All right.

389
00:41:33,866 --> 00:41:35,910
I'm sorry I couldn't tell you.

390
00:41:37,537 --> 00:41:38,830
Have you both been okay?

391
00:41:42,417 --> 00:41:43,418
Yes.

392
00:41:51,134 --> 00:41:54,512
So Lee Hwayoung was the officer
who let Min Junho get away

393
00:41:54,595 --> 00:41:58,057
when he tried to kill Kang Jisun
during the public manhunt?

394
00:41:58,725 --> 00:42:00,768
Even after firing her Taser at him?

395
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:04,981
Well, more importantly…

396
00:42:07,817 --> 00:42:09,152
-[keyboard clacks]
-[video stops]

397
00:42:18,995 --> 00:42:20,830
<i>There's no point resisting anyway, so…</i>

398
00:42:23,374 --> 00:42:25,376
-Wait, hold on.
-[keyboard clacks]

399
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:30,048
Is Kang Jisun actually
abducting Min Junho…

400
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,594
…in this car?

401
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:37,055
We found this on Min Junho's tablet.

402
00:42:38,931 --> 00:42:42,810
Inspector Lee had planted a GPS tracker
in Min Junho's car.

403
00:42:42,894 --> 00:42:46,606
She called me that day because
the car's location seemed suspicious.

404
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:48,399
And the next day…

405
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,528
Min Junho had a blood test done.

406
00:42:52,612 --> 00:42:54,489
TEST RESULTS REPORT

407
00:43:05,792 --> 00:43:09,128
So Kang Jisun drugged Min Junho
and abducted him…

408
00:43:11,214 --> 00:43:12,965
and Lee Hwayoung joined her?

409
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,557
<i>The car's location seemed suspicious,</i>

410
00:43:21,641 --> 00:43:23,309
so I went to check it out myself.

411
00:43:23,893 --> 00:43:27,772
If I hadn't,
Kang Jisun could've been in danger.

412
00:43:29,732 --> 00:43:35,113
There was no evidence that
she drugged or abducted him.

413
00:43:35,905 --> 00:43:40,284
-What I saw was Min Junho assaulting her.
-[Jisun struggling]

414
00:43:48,835 --> 00:43:49,877
Inspector Lee.

415
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:53,047
You've been keeping that a secret
all this time?

416
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:59,470
If Kang Jisun was the one being assaulted,

417
00:44:00,138 --> 00:44:02,306
why didn't she report it?

418
00:44:04,100 --> 00:44:06,978
Because she knew he'd get off
with a slap on the wrist.

419
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:09,730
And she was afraid he'd come after her.

420
00:44:20,992 --> 00:44:22,118
What's this?

421
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:24,453
[Duil] Min Junho had a blood test done
the next day.

422
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:29,917
[Myeongsu] Probably to preserve evidence
that Kang Jisun had drugged him with GHB,

423
00:44:30,001 --> 00:44:33,087
so he could use it against her
when the time came.

424
00:44:34,755 --> 00:44:36,007
Oh.

425
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:37,717
So is this how he intended to use it?

426
00:44:41,345 --> 00:44:46,809
Just because GHB was found in his blood
doesn't prove Jisun gave it to him.

427
00:44:47,727 --> 00:44:50,438
Just like finding GHB in my blood

428
00:44:50,521 --> 00:44:53,024
wasn't proof that Min Junho
had drugged me.

429
00:44:54,317 --> 00:44:55,526
Isn't that right, sir?

430
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:04,911
Fine, let's leave that aside for now.

431
00:45:06,412 --> 00:45:10,750
But I hear you also happened
to be the one who found Min Junho

432
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:13,294
when he came back to kill Kang Jisun,

433
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:15,129
shortly before his death?

434
00:45:15,838 --> 00:45:18,507
-I was on patrol.
-[Myeongsu] Mmm.

435
00:45:19,759 --> 00:45:21,677
Didn't you let him get away on purpose?

436
00:45:21,761 --> 00:45:23,221
Hands off! Now!

437
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:30,228
Why would I do that?

438
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:36,108
To follow Min Junho as he fled
and find out where he was hiding?

439
00:45:41,489 --> 00:45:42,698
And then what?

440
00:45:45,368 --> 00:45:48,204
Well, then…

441
00:45:49,497 --> 00:45:51,040
I was just thinking out loud.

442
00:45:53,501 --> 00:45:55,169
Regardless of what you have to say,

443
00:45:55,253 --> 00:45:57,964
you won't be able
to avoid disciplinary action

444
00:45:58,047 --> 00:46:00,925
for covering up a crime
related to Min Junho's abduction.

445
00:46:01,968 --> 00:46:03,636
But solving the murder takes priority,

446
00:46:03,719 --> 00:46:06,389
so for now, keep a low profile
and stay out of trouble.

447
00:46:38,671 --> 00:46:40,965
NO MURDER WEAPON FOUND

448
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:42,717
[Duil] Kang Jisun's got some nerve.

449
00:46:43,968 --> 00:46:48,639
Min must outweigh her
by at least twenty or thirty kilos…

450
00:46:50,016 --> 00:46:52,018
…but she still thought
she could abduct him on her own.

451
00:46:55,521 --> 00:46:57,440
Maybe she didn't do it alone.

452
00:47:01,068 --> 00:47:04,447
I think there's someone important
we've overlooked.

453
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:06,490
[Duil] Who?

454
00:47:09,201 --> 00:47:10,411
[Myeongsu] <i>Another suspect.</i>

455
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:17,668
-[box cutter clicks]
-[knocks on door]

456
00:47:17,752 --> 00:47:19,462
-Come in.
-[door opens]

457
00:47:19,545 --> 00:47:22,840
Sir, there are some police officers
here to see you.

458
00:47:25,426 --> 00:47:26,719
-What do they want?
-Well…

459
00:47:26,802 --> 00:47:27,803
Hello.

460
00:47:28,429 --> 00:47:30,056
Sorry to bother you.

461
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:32,350
Well…

462
00:47:32,433 --> 00:47:36,395
We're investigating Min Junho's death.

463
00:47:41,734 --> 00:47:44,278
How long have you been
seeing Ms. Kang Jisun?

464
00:47:45,071 --> 00:47:51,494
We became official only recently,
but we've known each other for a while.

465
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:55,039
Min Junho's very existence

466
00:47:55,122 --> 00:48:00,086
must have made you absolutely furious.

467
00:48:02,046 --> 00:48:05,966
Ever since you found out
what he'd done to your girlfriend.

468
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:10,888
Of course.

469
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:20,189
-But that doesn't mean I--
-When it came to Jang Dongchan…

470
00:48:22,024 --> 00:48:24,693
did you feel the same way?

471
00:48:35,788 --> 00:48:37,665
That was five years ago.

472
00:48:39,542 --> 00:48:41,085
You know what he did, don't you?

473
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:45,172
I know he was hospitalized
after what you did to him,

474
00:48:45,673 --> 00:48:49,427
and that you ended up with
an assault conviction because of it.

475
00:48:51,178 --> 00:48:52,555
I'm aware of all that.

476
00:48:57,143 --> 00:49:00,646
Where were you
between 3 a.m. and 4 a.m. on the 18th?

477
00:49:05,025 --> 00:49:09,155
I'd just gotten back from a work trip,
so I was home.

478
00:49:10,573 --> 00:49:13,534
Could we check your phone records,
credit card transactions,

479
00:49:13,617 --> 00:49:16,912
bank accounts,
and vehicle location history?

480
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:20,916
As long as it's all legal.

481
00:49:23,043 --> 00:49:25,296
I doubt you'll find anything.

482
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:27,465
You've met Min Junho before, haven't you?

483
00:49:30,676 --> 00:49:33,929
We crossed paths briefly at a restaurant.

484
00:49:34,513 --> 00:49:37,016
How did it feel when you saw him up close?

485
00:49:44,482 --> 00:49:46,317
I was pretty far away,

486
00:49:47,401 --> 00:49:48,777
so I don't really remember.

487
00:49:57,620 --> 00:49:58,787
What do you think?

488
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:01,123
Nothing really stood out to me.

489
00:50:01,749 --> 00:50:05,794
Didn't you notice how neatly
everything on his desk was lined up?

490
00:50:09,548 --> 00:50:11,800
When a man falls hard for someone
later in life,

491
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:14,637
love can blind him to everything else.

492
00:50:15,554 --> 00:50:19,141
And when someone who's rigid
and always plays by the rules snaps,

493
00:50:19,642 --> 00:50:21,352
things can get ugly.

494
00:50:22,228 --> 00:50:23,229
So…

495
00:50:24,813 --> 00:50:28,108
you think he killed Min Junho
for his girlfriend?

496
00:50:29,902 --> 00:50:30,903
We don't know yet.

497
00:50:30,986 --> 00:50:32,988
You've got quite a reputation, you know.

498
00:50:33,989 --> 00:50:38,410
A 100% arrest rate because you always find
a way to pin the crime on someone.

499
00:50:52,967 --> 00:50:54,468
You haven't eaten, have you?

500
00:50:55,761 --> 00:50:58,430
They were selling these
outside the hospital.

501
00:50:58,514 --> 00:51:00,224
You love squid <i>sundae</i>.

502
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:04,061
Hey… Why did you come all the way here?

503
00:51:06,230 --> 00:51:07,231
Well…

504
00:51:09,108 --> 00:51:10,943
I wanted to get some fresh air too.

505
00:51:19,034 --> 00:51:20,703
Where did you go the other night?

506
00:51:23,539 --> 00:51:27,126
-I woke up early in the--
-I just stepped out for a bit. That's all.

507
00:51:31,213 --> 00:51:33,299
I've been having trouble
falling asleep lately.

508
00:51:37,678 --> 00:51:39,847
I've been blaming you
this whole time, but…

509
00:51:47,021 --> 00:51:49,231
That's how Min Junho operated.

510
00:51:49,857 --> 00:51:52,776
He made me believe I'd gotten drunk
and made a mistake.

511
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:55,863
We both fell for it.

512
00:52:10,919 --> 00:52:13,714
Why don't you go on inside?
I'll finish up here and be right in.

513
00:52:21,263 --> 00:52:22,348
Smells delicious.

514
00:52:27,394 --> 00:52:28,395
Go on inside.

515
00:52:30,272 --> 00:52:31,357
I'll be right there.

516
00:53:17,236 --> 00:53:18,570
The phone records.

517
00:53:46,306 --> 00:53:47,349
Hello.

518
00:53:48,350 --> 00:53:49,351
What's this about?

519
00:53:50,561 --> 00:53:52,438
We have a search and seizure warrant.

520
00:53:54,148 --> 00:53:55,441
A search and seizure warrant?

521
00:53:55,524 --> 00:53:57,735
[Myeongsu] It's quite an interesting read,
so take your time.

522
00:53:57,818 --> 00:53:59,945
We'll have a look around the house
while you do.

523
00:54:00,529 --> 00:54:01,572
Here, take it.

524
00:54:02,573 --> 00:54:03,615
-Here.
-What…

525
00:54:08,704 --> 00:54:10,038
-Over here.
-[officer] Yes, sir.

526
00:54:11,373 --> 00:54:12,750
What's this about?

527
00:54:13,250 --> 00:54:14,626
You lied to us.

528
00:54:15,544 --> 00:54:18,422
We've confirmed that your phone
was near Sangcheon Port

529
00:54:18,505 --> 00:54:21,633
around the time Min Junho died.

530
00:54:25,596 --> 00:54:28,849
And four months ago, you drugged Min Junho
with GHB and abducted him,

531
00:54:28,932 --> 00:54:31,226
taking him to the docks, didn't you?

532
00:54:34,646 --> 00:54:35,773
That was…

533
00:54:37,065 --> 00:54:38,150
That was what?

534
00:54:41,320 --> 00:54:44,364
Did you really think
you could keep it a secret forever?

535
00:54:48,619 --> 00:54:49,620
Finished reading?

536
00:55:02,758 --> 00:55:05,302
Start with the bookshelf over there.

537
00:55:11,433 --> 00:55:13,435
Your car's included
in the search warrant too,

538
00:55:13,519 --> 00:55:16,021
so just leave your keys where they are,
all right?

539
00:55:24,780 --> 00:55:26,657
Oh, right. Your phone too.

540
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:32,704
Well, right here…

541
00:55:34,581 --> 00:55:36,458
Here it is. Right here.

542
00:55:37,084 --> 00:55:38,377
"Cell phone."

543
00:56:01,525 --> 00:56:02,776
Thank you.

544
00:56:02,859 --> 00:56:04,403
-Hey.
-[officer] Yes, sir.

545
00:56:07,155 --> 00:56:08,907
You're welcome to stay and watch.

546
00:56:31,638 --> 00:56:32,931
How could they do this?

547
00:56:36,184 --> 00:56:37,936
Something like this was bound to happen.

548
00:56:38,020 --> 00:56:41,857
-I'm the victim. How could they--
-Because the culprit was murdered.

549
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:44,693
This is a murder investigation.

550
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:48,530
If they have their suspicions,
it might be better to clear them up now.

551
00:56:48,614 --> 00:56:50,449
Do you realize how naive that sounds?

552
00:56:51,033 --> 00:56:53,452
The police didn't believe me
last time either!

553
00:56:59,333 --> 00:57:01,335
The police are just doing their job.

554
00:57:02,628 --> 00:57:04,463
You'll be fine.

555
00:57:05,047 --> 00:57:07,090
You had nothing to do with the murder.

556
00:57:26,985 --> 00:57:29,029
Detective Hwang is suspecting us.

557
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:34,743
He doesn't leave cases unsolved.
He always finds someone to arrest.

558
00:57:36,536 --> 00:57:38,121
Even if he has to frame someone.

559
00:57:41,958 --> 00:57:43,085
Then what do we do?

560
00:57:43,168 --> 00:57:45,128
[Hwayoung] We can't give him
anything to use against us.

561
00:57:46,838 --> 00:57:49,132
Don't do anything
that might raise more suspicions.

562
00:57:49,675 --> 00:57:51,760
And try not to come see me either.

563
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:53,553
At least until the case is closed.

564
00:58:17,953 --> 00:58:19,162
[Namu] Are you okay?

565
00:58:21,498 --> 00:58:24,668
[Jisun] The day I first reported it
to the police, my sister said to me…

566
00:58:27,879 --> 00:58:30,257
that it would all be over after that day.

567
00:58:36,221 --> 00:58:38,890
But I'm starting to think
it might never be over.

568
00:58:41,184 --> 00:58:42,352
The police…

569
00:58:44,396 --> 00:58:46,481
They came to my office too.

570
00:58:49,776 --> 00:58:50,861
I'm sorry.

571
00:58:52,112 --> 00:58:53,280
[Namu] No.

572
00:58:54,448 --> 00:58:56,199
You have nothing to be sorry about.

573
00:58:58,368 --> 00:58:59,786
Have you found a lawyer?

574
00:59:01,371 --> 00:59:02,622
I'm innocent.

575
00:59:04,166 --> 00:59:06,168
I know, but just in case, I'll ask around.

576
00:59:06,251 --> 00:59:07,586
You don't have to.

577
00:59:13,675 --> 00:59:15,469
What did the police ask you?

578
00:59:17,971 --> 00:59:20,557
[Namu exclaims] Just…

579
00:59:22,267 --> 00:59:24,227
Some ordinary questions
about our relationship.

580
00:59:28,982 --> 00:59:30,484
I'm really sorry.

581
00:59:31,443 --> 00:59:34,029
For dragging you into this mess too.

582
00:59:58,512 --> 01:00:00,430
[Jisun] <i>You're a good man, Namu.</i>

583
01:00:05,352 --> 01:00:07,646
<i>But I don't think</i>
<i>the timing is right for us.</i>

584
01:00:10,774 --> 01:00:14,986
I think we should end things
before they get any more complicated.

585
01:00:19,407 --> 01:00:22,035
That way, you won't get hurt
any more than you already have.

586
01:00:24,788 --> 01:00:25,789
[Namu] I…

587
01:00:27,624 --> 01:00:29,084
I thought that

588
01:00:29,709 --> 01:00:33,463
as long as we were together,
we could overcome anything.

589
01:00:43,306 --> 01:00:44,307
[officer] Sir.

590
01:00:45,058 --> 01:00:46,101
[Duil] What is it?

591
01:00:59,447 --> 01:01:01,616
[Namu] Everything you've done…

592
01:01:04,828 --> 01:01:06,329
every choice you've made…

593
01:01:11,918 --> 01:01:13,378
I understand it all.

594
01:01:30,061 --> 01:01:32,188
I just hope you find some peace, Jisun.

595
01:01:36,276 --> 01:01:37,569
But still…

596
01:01:39,237 --> 01:01:40,447
if you ever need me,

597
01:01:41,489 --> 01:01:42,949
don't hesitate to call.

598
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:55,712
[Myeongsu] Still can't believe
a victim can turn into a suspect?

599
01:02:01,259 --> 01:02:02,260
[Jisun] Are you done?

600
01:02:03,219 --> 01:02:04,346
[Duil] Yes.

601
01:02:04,429 --> 01:02:06,890
[Myeongsu] But for you, Kang Jisun,
this is just the beginning.

602
01:02:06,973 --> 01:02:08,058
What do you mean?

603
01:02:09,517 --> 01:02:11,269
We need you to come down to the station.

604
01:02:12,771 --> 01:02:13,980
Why?

605
01:02:14,064 --> 01:02:16,608
Because we found something
that shouldn't have been there.

606
01:02:19,486 --> 01:02:21,363
-What?
-[Myeongsu] Kang Jisun.

607
01:02:23,490 --> 01:02:24,699
You're under arrest.

608
01:02:28,328 --> 01:02:30,705
-On what charge?
-For the murder of Min Junho.

609
01:02:38,213 --> 01:02:42,133
THE PERFECT LIE

610
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:12,455
[Myeongsu] <i>Because no one is ever</i>
<i>completely above suspicion.</i>

611
01:03:12,539 --> 01:03:14,749
Someone must be trying to frame me…

612
01:03:14,833 --> 01:03:17,627
You're the one who destroyed evidence.

613
01:03:18,962 --> 01:03:20,338
[Jisun] What was that photo?

614
01:03:20,422 --> 01:03:22,090
Since you're not telling me the truth,

615
01:03:22,173 --> 01:03:24,968
it's only fair that I keep quiet
about Kim Namu too.

616
01:03:25,051 --> 01:03:26,970
You do know
what Min Junho was like, right?

617
01:03:27,053 --> 01:03:28,680
[Junho] <i>I'm going to live a new life.</i>

618
01:03:29,431 --> 01:03:31,182
-[tires screeching]
-[Jisun] <i>Hyunsoo!</i>

619
01:03:31,266 --> 01:03:32,809
[Junho] <i>As if I've been born again.</i>

620
01:03:32,892 --> 01:03:34,394
[Duil] <i>This is all a coincidence?</i>

621
01:03:34,477 --> 01:03:35,645
[Myeongsu] <i>These people.</i>

622
01:03:35,729 --> 01:03:39,482
<i>They all knew Min Junho was hiding there.</i>

623
01:03:41,109 --> 01:03:43,361
How do I know you didn't fabricate that?

624
01:03:45,155 --> 01:03:46,698
I didn't kill Min Junho.

625
01:04:03,089 --> 01:04:04,674
THE PERFECT LIE

626
01:04:04,758 --> 01:04:06,760
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
